\subsubsection{Audit Logs}
The audit logs provide:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{User Activity}: Record of user actions within the system
    \item \textbf{System Events}: Automated system actions and processes
    \item \textbf{Access Attempts}: Successful and failed login attempts
    \item \textbf{Configuration Changes}: Record of changes to system settings
\end{itemize}

These logs can be filtered, searched, and exported for compliance and security analysis.

\section{Operational Procedures}
\label{sec:operational-procedures}

This section outlines common operational procedures for users of the Nebula Power platform.

\subsection{Installation Management}
\label{subsec:installation-management}

\subsubsection{Adding a New Installation}
To add a new solar installation to the system:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Navigate to the Installations section and select "Add New Installation"
    \item Enter basic installation details:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Installation name
        \item Physical location (address and/or GPS coordinates)
        \item Customer information
        \item Installation date
    \end{itemize}
    \item Enter technical specifications:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Solar panel type and quantity
        \item Inverter model and specifications
        \item Battery capacity (if applicable)
        \item Maximum power output
    \end{itemize}
    \item Assign payment plan to the installation
    \item Register monitoring devices (see next section)
    \item Activate the installation
\end{enumerate}

\subsubsection{Registering Devices}
To register a monitoring device:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item In the installation details page, select "Add Device"
    \item Enter device information:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Device type (inverter, meter, communication module, etc.)
        \item Serial number
        \item Firmware version
    \end{itemize}
    \item Generate or enter a unique device token for secure communication
    \item Configure device communication settings:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Communication protocol
        \item Data transmission frequency
        \item Connection parameters
    \end{itemize}
    \item Activate the device and verify communication
\end{enumerate}

\subsubsection{Decommissioning an Installation}
To decommission an installation:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Verify that all payment obligations have been fulfilled
    \item Navigate to the installation details and select "Decommission"
    \item Provide reason for decommissioning
    \item Specify decommissioning date
    \item Confirm decommissioning action (requires administrative privileges)
    \item Generate decommissioning report
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{User Management}
\label{subsec:user-management-ops}

\subsubsection{Creating User Accounts}
Administrators can create new user accounts:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Navigate to User Management and select "Add User"
    \item Enter user information:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Email address
        \item Full name
        \item Contact information
        \item User role
    \end{itemize}
    \item Assign permissions and access levels
    \item Generate temporary password
    \item Send invitation email to the new user
\end{enumerate}

\subsubsection{Managing Roles and Permissions}
To modify user roles and permissions:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Navigate to User Management and select the user
    \item Select "Edit Roles and Permissions"
    \item Modify role assignments or individual permissions
    \item Provide reason for the change
    \item Save changes and notify the user if necessary
\end{enumerate}

\subsubsection{Deactivating User Accounts}
To deactivate a user account:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Navigate to User Management and select the user
    \item Select "Deactivate Account"
    \item Provide reason for deactivation
    \item Specify if deactivation is temporary or permanent
    \item Confirm deactivation action
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Payment Operations}
\label{subsec:payment-operations}

\subsubsection{Creating Payment Plans}
To create a new payment plan:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Navigate to Payment Management and select "Create Plan"
    \item Configure plan parameters:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Plan name and description
        \item Payment amount and frequency
        \item Total number of payments or contract duration
        \item Grace period settings
        \item Late payment penalties
    \end{itemize}
    \item Set eligibility criteria (if applicable)
    \item Define activation and expiration dates
    \item Save and activate the plan
\end{enumerate}

\subsubsection{Processing Manual Payments}
To record a manual payment:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Navigate to the customer's payment history
    \item Select "Record Manual Payment"
    \item Enter payment details:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Payment amount
        \item Payment date
        \item Payment method
        \item Reference number or transaction ID
    \end{itemize}
    \item Upload receipt or proof of payment (if available)
    \item Confirm and process the payment
\end{enumerate}

\subsubsection{Managing Overdue Payments}
To handle overdue payments:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Navigate to Payment Management and filter for overdue payments
    \item Select the overdue payment
    \item Choose an appropriate action:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Send payment reminder
        \item Apply late payment fee
        \item Extend grace period
        \item Initiate service restriction
        \item Create payment plan modification
    \end{itemize}
    \item Document the action and any customer communication
    \item Monitor for payment resolution
\end{enumerate}

\section{Troubleshooting}
\label{sec:troubleshooting}

This section provides guidance for resolving common issues encountered when using the Nebula Power platform.

\subsection{Login and Access Issues}
\label{subsec:login-issues}

\begin{table}[h]
    \centering
    \begin{tabular}{|p{5cm}|p{9cm}|}
        \hline
        \textbf{Issue} & \textbf{Resolution} \\
        \hline
        Unable to log in with correct credentials & 
        • Verify that the email address is entered correctly\\
        • Check if Caps Lock is enabled\\
        • Clear browser cache and cookies\\
        • Try resetting password\\
        • Contact system administrator if issue persists \\
        \hline
        Account locked after multiple failed attempts & 
        • Wait for the automatic unlock period (typically 30 minutes)\\
        • Use the "Forgot Password" function to reset password\\
        • Contact system administrator for manual account unlock \\
        \hline
        Multi-factor authentication (MFA) issues & 
        • Ensure device time is correctly synchronized\\
        • Verify that the correct MFA code is being entered\\
        • Use backup codes if available\\
        • Contact system administrator for MFA reset \\
        \hline
        Missing access to expected features & 
        • Verify that your user role includes the required permissions\\
        • Check if the feature requires specific subscription level\\
        • Log out and log back in to refresh permissions\\
        • Contact system administrator to review access rights \\
        \hline
    \end{tabular}
    \caption{Login and access troubleshooting guide}
    \label{tab:login-troubleshooting}
\end{table}

\subsection{Data Connectivity Issues}
\label{subsec:connectivity-issues}

\begin{table}[h]
    \centering
    \begin{tabular}{|p{5cm}|p{9cm}|}
        \hline
        \textbf{Issue} & \textbf{Resolution} \\
        \hline
        No data from solar installation & 
        • Check power supply to monitoring device\\
        • Verify network connectivity at installation site\\
        • Check for cellular signal strength if using cellular connection\\
        • Restart monitoring device\\
        • Check server connectivity\\
        • Verify device registration status \\
        \hline
        Delayed or intermittent data & 
        • Check network connection quality\\
        • Verify data transmission frequency settings\\
        • Check for interference sources\\
        • Update device firmware if available\\
        • Adjust data buffering settings \\
        \hline
        Data discrepancies between reports & 
        • Check time zone settings\\
        • Verify reporting period boundaries\\
        • Check for data aggregation differences\\
        • Look for filtering applied to different reports\\
        • Verify data synchronization status \\
        \hline
    \end{tabular}
    \caption{Data connectivity troubleshooting guide}
    \label{tab:connectivity-troubleshooting}
\end{table}

\subsection{Payment Processing Issues}
\label{subsec:payment-issues}

\begin{table}[h]
    \centering
    \begin{tabular}{|p{5cm}|p{9cm}|}
        \hline
        \textbf{Issue} & \textbf{Resolution} \\
        \hline
        Payment not registered in system & 
        • Verify payment was completed successfully\\
        • Check transaction ID or reference number\\
        • Allow time for payment processing (typically 1-2 business days)\\
        • Contact financial institution to confirm transaction status\\
        • Submit payment proof to customer support \\
        \hline
        Incorrect payment amount recorded & 
        • Provide transaction receipt or proof of payment\\
        • Check for partial payments or pending transactions\\
        • Verify if fees or penalties were applied\\
        • Contact customer support with detailed payment information \\
        \hline
        Unable to make online payment & 
        • Check internet connection\\
        • Verify payment method is valid and has sufficient funds\\
        • Clear browser cache or try a different browser\\
        • Check if payment gateway is experiencing issues\\
        • Try an alternative payment method\\
        • Contact customer support \\
        \hline
    \end{tabular}
    \caption{Payment processing troubleshooting guide}
    \label{tab:payment-troubleshooting}
\end{table}

\subsection{False Security Alerts}
\label{subsec:false-alerts}

\begin{table}[h]
    \centering
    \begin{tabular}{|p{5cm}|p{9cm}|}
        \hline
        \textbf{Issue} & \textbf{Resolution} \\
        \hline
        False tampering detection & 
        • Verify if maintenance was being performed\\
        • Check for environmental factors (severe weather, etc.)\\
        • Inspect physical installation for damage or disturbance\\
        • Adjust tampering sensitivity if authorized\\
        • Document the false alarm with photos if possible\\
        • Mark alert as false positive in the system \\
        \hline
        Multiple consecutive alerts & 
        • Check for pattern or common trigger\\
        • Verify if alerts occur at specific times\\
        • Check for environmental factors\\
        • Request technician inspection if persistent\\
        • Temporarily adjust alert thresholds if authorized \\
        \hline
    \end{tabular}
    \caption{Security alert troubleshooting guide}
    \label{tab:alert-troubleshooting}
\end{table}

\section{Reference}
\label{sec:reference}

This section provides reference information for users of the Nebula Power platform.

\subsection{Glossary}
\label{subsec:glossary}

\begin{description}
    \item[API] Application Programming Interface - A set of rules and protocols for building and interacting with software applications.
    \item[Authentication] The process of verifying the identity of a user or device.
    \item[Authorization] The process of determining what permissions a user has once authenticated.
    \item[Dashboard] A visual interface showing key metrics and status information.
    \item[Device Token] A unique identifier used to authenticate a device with the system.
    \item[Inverter] A device that converts DC electricity from solar panels into AC electricity for home use or grid export.
    \item[kWh (Kilowatt-hour)] A unit of energy equal to 1,000 watt-hours, used to measure electricity consumption and production.
    \item[MFA (Multi-Factor Authentication)] An authentication method requiring users to provide two or more verification factors.
    \item[PAYG (Pay-As-You-Go)] A financing model where customers pay for solar systems in installments as they use them.
    \item[PV (Photovoltaic)] Technology that converts sunlight directly into electricity using semiconductor materials.
    \item[Tampering] Unauthorized modification or interference with a solar installation or monitoring equipment.
    \item[Yield] The amount of electrical energy produced by a solar installation over a specific period.
\end{description}

